    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe stored `registrationDate` is already business-day-adjusted by the controller, so all three fiscal-year\u2013derived values compute off it. I moved them to a fiscal year that starts on **1 July** (Australian convention \u2014 July\u2013Dec belongs to the *next* calendar year's FY; e.g. 2025-08-01 and 2026-03-01 both \u2192 FY26).\n\n**`Owner.java`**\n- Added `fiscalYearOf(LocalDate)` \u2014 the single date\u2192fiscal-year mapping: `month >= 7 ? year + 1 : year`.\n- Added `getFiscalYear()` returning `FY<YY>` (last two digits of the fiscal year), or `null` when there's no registration date.\n- `getMembershipNumber()` now uses the fiscal-year `YY` for the identifier's year segment instead of `registrationDate.getYear() % 100`.\n- `hasLongTenure(...)` now counts **elapsed fiscal years** (`fiscalYearOf(asOf) - fiscalYearOf(registrationDate) > 1`) instead of a 365-day window; a newly created owner still has zero tenure, so tenure points are never awarded on creation.\n- Removed the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import and updated the membership-points doc.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** (source for the generated `OwnerDto`; MapStruct auto-maps the matching getters)\n- Added the read-only `fiscalYear` field.\n- Updated `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to the fiscal-year basis.\n\nThe acceptance test (`fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`) passes, and I verified the behaviour change in the audit log: an owner registered 2026-09-10 now gets `membershipNumber=\u2026-M27` (FY27), whereas the old calendar-year rule would have produced `-M26`.",
